---@alias lrocket.TargetRule table

---@alias lrocket.boolean 'yes'|'no'|boolean

---@class lrocket.BuildConf
---@field entrypoint string? :required: Main lua file
---@field output string? Output filename
---@field otype string? Output file format
---@field modpath searchpath[]? List of module search paths in the format `<lang>:<searchpath>` (where `<lang>` is one of: `lua,shared,static,c,teal,<custom>`)
---@field modules string[]? Explicitly include the specified modules
---@field exclude string[]? Exclude given modules from search
---@field optional string[]? Include these optional modules.<br/><br/>This argument enables optional module parsing for specified statements (using `[x]pcall`)
---@field liblua 'shared'|'static'? default: 'static' - Variant of the Lua library to link against
---@field debug 'all'|'project'|'module'? Add debugging information to the output file
---@field optimize 'space'|'speed'? Enable optimizations
---@field fuzzy lrocket.boolean? default: true - Examine complex require statements when resolving modules
---@field runtime_path string? Runtime `LUA_PATH` used for lua modules (supports `??` and `!`)
---@field runtime_cpath string? Runtime `LUA_CPATH` used for lua modules (supports `??` and `!`)
---@field keep lrocket.boolean? Do not remove intermediate C code after compilation
---@field link_sibling_deps lrocket.boolean? default: true - Resolve dynamic dependencies of statically linked lua modules by scanning equally named dynamic modules
---@field copy_native_libs lrocket.boolean? default: true - Copies required shared C libraries to the output directory
---@field windows_gui lrocket.boolean? Link with `/SUBSYSTEM:WINDOWS` (or `-mwindows` for MinGW)
---@field modname string? (for otype `shared`) - Module name of the shared library, used for `luaopen_<modname>`
---@field export string[]? (for otype `shared`) - Export additional `luaopen_<modname>` (supports globs)
---@field cconf lrocket.CompilerConf? :internal:
---@field trees string[]? :internal:

---@class lrocket.DebugConf
---@field log_level string|integer? lrocket compiler: level of verbosity
---@field warnmode 'error'|'warn'? Decides whether warnings should warn or throw an error
---@field perf lrocket.boolean? Show instrumentalized timings
---@field perf_log string? Log profiling stacktraces to this file (flamegraph format)

